1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
Stand up tall, reach out your hand.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,880
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:11,240
The paint within brings
out a map of your own.

4
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:19,680
To the left and the right,
all we saw stormy nights.

5
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:22,960
All the rough winds and
waves coming day after day.

6
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,220
And the values we had
were about to collapse.

7
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:28,777
Oh, just where do we go next?

8
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:35,420
And as we look down to the compass in
hand Is it showing us the right direction?

9
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,617
All we know is nobody
here knows it for certain.

10
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,937
So close your eyes and breathe in deeply.

11
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:45,177
And listen to your soul.

12
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:48,117
You'll see a path in front of you.

13
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,537
And you'll know just where you need to go.

14
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:55,817
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

15
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,037
Cut through the wind and make us stand.

16
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,900
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

17
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:08,137
I'll do it my own way,
that's what's best for me.

18
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:11,777
And you do it your way,
that's how it's got to be.

19
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:15,377
We're moving forward, now I'm ready.

20
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:19,217
But at times it's okay
to get help on the way.

21
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,757
For the future ahead, burning bright.

22
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:24,217
For what's ahead you see.

23
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:27,600
Is beyond your wildest dreams.

24
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,757
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

25
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,977
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

26
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:38,800
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

27
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:44,077
We'll do it our way,
the best that we know.

28
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:45,577
With tears and doubts and tone.

29
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:47,957
We'll go where we all wanna go.

30
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:52,320
The page within brings colors of our own.

31
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:06,620
I'll make you nice and toasty.

32
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,400
I'll make you nice and crispy.

33
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,037
I'll make you nice and bloody.

34
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:18,097
Ma-ma-ma-ma...

35
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:21,600
Ma-ma-ma-ma...

36
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:33,488
Please take me straight
to the inner castle.

37
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:36,537
You're making me fly you
around when I'm injured, huh?

38
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:38,091
This better be important.

39
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,697
I'm just worried.

40
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:41,977
Hopefully it's nothing.

41
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:44,677
But the Beast Pirate
said that some sort of

42
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:47,277
giant apparition appeared
on the second floor.

43
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,948
What does that mean for us?

44
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,894
It's spreading fire through the castle.

45
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:59,860
Be ready for the worst. Always.

46
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:09,980
Run away!

47
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,397
The monster's coming!

48
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,715
The Ten Samurai are blocking the exit!

49
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:16,300
We're stuck! Step back! We got a cannon!

50
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:19,021
The fire is spreading everywhere!

51
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,580
Secure an escape route!

52
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,637
They're through those samurai!

53
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,550
Hurry!

54
00:03:23,633 --> 00:03:26,207
Let's get out of here
or we'll burn to death!

55
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,860
I'm telling you, young
master, it's a sweet deal!

56
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,060
Hear me out for a sec!

57
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:39,926
You won't regret it, I swear!

58
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:46,597
Moving on to the next
target, you little weasel.

59
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:49,856
I don't buy into your plans
so you suck up the Yamato.

60
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:51,160
Young master!

61
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:52,980
Stop the poo!

62
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,817
I told you I have somewhere to be!

63
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:56,180
Stop following me!

64
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:58,040
Fuga, Fuga!

65
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,500
Sorry, Fuga.

66
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:05,637
I didn't mean to yell at you
back there, but I'm in a hurry!

67
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:06,600
Fuga, Fuga!

68
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:09,571
I sure wish I could be as carefree as you.

69
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:13,300
This is an urgent report
for all castle floors.

70
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:18,227
The giant plane creature is
currently headed for the basement.

71
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:24,390
Huh?

72
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:27,180
A cushion? Not quite.

73
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,920
They're hairs, but I don't know whose.

74
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:32,280
Well, that's odd. Fugle?

75
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:33,580
Are you ready?

76
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,150
Ready.

77
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:37,820
Don't move!

78
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:42,220
It seems we have to fight!

79
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:47,370
Fight!

80
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:52,750
Uh...

81
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:54,370
Robin?

82
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,980
What is that thing?

83
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,700
A ball of flames.

84
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,260
What a nuisance.

85
00:05:09,540 --> 00:05:10,460
What the hell?

86
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,100
It's mute!

87
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:16,701
The slave creature's
intentions are still unknown.

88
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:22,880
Brother, run! It's coming! Hold on!

89
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:27,406
Right now, it's descending through
the floors at a steady pace.

90
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:31,360
It seems impervious to attack.

91
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,040
Take extreme caution!

92
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,440
He's pulling his crust.

93
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:05,644
Is he trying to make fun of me?

94
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,440
What the hell is this?

95
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:10,910
Ready!

96
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:14,080
Impurious Deepline State!

97
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:20,980
I hit like a laser beam!

98
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,731
It's impossible to block!

99
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:28,760
In ancient times, this is
how Pteranodons hunted.

100
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:31,500
And now, you're my prey!

101
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,560
Damn, I don't know my dinosaurs.

102
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:59,686
I gotta hit him with something
or he's just gonna wear me down.

103
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:05,640
So, I'm guessing that flame on your back
must be a Pteranodon thing, too, huh?

104
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:07,890
That's stupid.

105
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,589
Hey, you're the one
with the stupid powers!

106
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:15,877
He's just gonna keep trash-talking
till he picks me off.

107
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:18,725
It's time to knock that
bastard out of the sky.

108
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:40,660
Three-sword style, black
rope, great Tatsumaki!

109
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,920
That didn't even leave a dent.

110
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,927
What the hell is he made of?

111
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:04,040
So, dinosaurs have skin tough as steel.

112
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,633
Just like dragons, huh?

113
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:08,500
I have far more than just tough skin.

114
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:11,800
My powers are unique.

115
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:16,920
I'll give you a sword fight if you want.

116
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,140
I do enjoy a good duel.

117
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,780
I cut him, but he doesn't bleed.

118
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:33,720
Drunk Tiger!

119
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:41,337
His wings are strong.

120
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,760
They're agile too.

121
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:47,580
Seems like he uses them
more to attack than fly.

122
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,360
The flame on his back keeps burning.

123
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:58,945
I thought that was part of his
Devil Fruit power, but maybe not.

124
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:03,840
He could be a fishman, a parked
giant, or anything under that mask.

125
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:07,137
Hell, he might even be
something I've never heard of.

126
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:09,640
I see confusion in your eyes.

127
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,746
You're looking for an answer.

128
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:21,380
This is not good.

129
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:25,080
I have to think.

130
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:28,440
If I can't figure him out.

131
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,320
I'm screwed.

132
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:38,160
There's no way I can beat him like this.

133
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:56,920
What's that sound?

134
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,060
Show me something.

135
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:04,571
I must be hearing things.

136
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:23,500
What the hell's going on?

137
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:29,640
Ah, damn it, Enmo!

138
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:37,120
Hmm? Music?

139
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:45,020
Someone is playing a
charme scene, but why?

140
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,240
This is a battleground.

141
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:48,620
This is hell.

142
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:55,500
It's coming from the room
next door Is it an enemy?

143
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:01,440
Who is it?

144
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:02,857
The banquet is over.

145
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:05,234
They should be running for their lives!

146
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,277
It's too bright.

147
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:10,020
I can't see.

148
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,360
It can't be.

149
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:27,210
Toborosaki!

150
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,320
I'm dreaming, aren't I?

151
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:36,080
Either that or I'm dead.

152
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:42,980
I've thought about you every
night since that terrible day.

153
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:46,560
You've never left my mind
for an instant, my dear.

154
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:51,800
Nor have you left my mind, my lord.

155
00:11:56,340 --> 00:12:00,940
I promise I will be by your
side until the very end.

156
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:07,300
If this is a dream, I
don't want to wake up!

157
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:32,400
What is that?

158
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:34,305
It's moving through the walls.

159
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:49,337
Into the abyss...

160
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:51,140
Into the abyss!

161
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:56,120
Shoot it!

162
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:02,880
This is a message to all fours!

163
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:06,017
The flame creature is continuing
its descent to the basement!

164
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:09,218
The fire is spreading along
with it, so make caution!

165
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,637
A flame creature?

166
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:15,260
And it's headed down!

167
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:18,625
At this rate, it'll reach
the armory before me.

168
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:23,400
This is about to be a disaster.

169
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:26,826
It's going to set off
all of those explosives.

170
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:30,960
I have to hurry.

171
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:32,490
Fuga!

172
00:13:32,573 --> 00:13:34,854
Can you help me with something, please?

173
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,220
Fuga! This way!

174
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:39,280
Just follow me! Fuga!

175
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,540
If I had it my way,

176
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:47,111
I'd take a nap in this fellow's hair
and wake up when this disaster is over.

177
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:49,380
But life's not so simple, is it?

178
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:56,786
We've bought some time,
but they can't be far.

179
00:13:56,900 --> 00:13:58,617
Then they'll be after us soon.

180
00:13:58,700 --> 00:13:59,641
We should hurry.

181
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,620
There's nowhere to run.

182
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:32,500
We'll catch you soon enough.

183
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,040
Give me a smile.

184
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:43,789
You'll be front page news.

185
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:48,680
Lapdogs of the Celestial Dragon
spotted at Kaido's castle.

186
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:50,560
Now that's a scoop, boy!

187
00:14:55,620 --> 00:15:00,032
One little call to Morgan's and this
pirate's gonna be rolling in the dome.

188
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,380
Ooh, yeah, ooh, ooh, that's a good sign.

189
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:05,133
Well, I can see it now.

190
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:10,300
After losing their arms brokered
Doflamingo, the government makes their play.

191
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:30,760
Hey, Apoo!

192
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:35,480
Diaz Drake.

193
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:39,620
I know exactly who you are
and what you're trying to do.

194
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:42,841
Then you'd better cook up
a damn good cover story.

195
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:48,900
How inconvenient.

196
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,880
I'll erase you.

197
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:58,740
You're welcome.

198
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:08,940
That hurt!

199
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,020
Bunch of pugs!

200
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:13,780
You stinking assassins can suck it!

201
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:20,480
I thought for sure they
struck you dead. Oh, shut up!

202
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:23,641
I got Armament Haki just
like anyone else, okay?

203
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:26,274
They're gonna pay for screwing with me!

204
00:16:27,740 --> 00:16:31,560
I can't believe I just saved some
dumbass traitor from the Navy.

205
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:32,820
Stop yapping.

206
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:35,893
Are you gonna end this, or is it all me?

207
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,190
End it?

208
00:16:37,273 --> 00:16:38,700
I didn't even start it, man!

209
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:40,220
Yes, you did.

210
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:41,520
These guys suck.

211
00:16:41,820 --> 00:16:43,840
You better believe I'll fight.

212
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:45,100
No!

213
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:59,120
No! Bk-bk-bk!

214
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:14,674
Why is this happening?

215
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,520
Hey, Enma!

216
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:21,220
I didn't say you could unleash your power!

217
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:23,620
You listen to me!

218
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,920
How sad.

219
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:33,480
Happy of falling out.

220
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:12,577
what are you staring at I'll give you one

221
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:16,357
chance now show me your

222
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:21,000
worst you ask for it

223
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:32,940
Jackpaw. What?

224
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:49,917
Sorry to eavesdrop, but you were talking
to the pirate hunter, weren't you?

225
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,706
That guy's never going
to be king, by the way.

226
00:19:00,260 --> 00:19:01,277
That was close.

227
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:04,260
I'd be dead if I didn't
use my armament in Haki.

228
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:20,537
That was one hell of an explosion.

229
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:22,561
Was he planning on dying with me?

230
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:25,280
That looked like a suicide attack.

231
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:28,460
except he doesn't have a scratch on him.

232
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:36,600
King is a Lunarian, a race that was
thought to have gone extinct long ago.

233
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:41,099
They're monsters who are able to
survive in all natural environments.

234
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:46,420
In the past, they were known as gods if
you want an idea of how strong they are.

235
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:49,700
If they're so special, why
did they become extinct?

236
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:51,900
I am a scientist!

237
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:56,220
Not a history kick!

238
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:11,180
One sword style. E .I.

239
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:17,580
Death.

240
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:20,160
I am some.

241
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:38,200
Oh, my God.

242
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:54,180
I didn't face him at all.

243
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:58,676
I keep ramping up, but you
don't even bother to block.

244
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:07,180
The music again.

245
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:16,740
Oh, Emma, wait!

246
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:20,100
Hear your deep pride! Stay!

247
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:24,820
Jakuna can be killed!

248
00:21:43,780 --> 00:21:46,960
A swordsman getting held
back by his own sword.

249
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:48,760
Now that's a sight.

250
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:07,397
The sword's cursed I think I'll take it.

251
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:10,457
No I can't sell it because
if something happens to you

252
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:13,177
with that sword the curse could
come back to me you idiot.

253
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:17,400
Yeah then how's this
we'll play a little game?

254
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:34,500
Yeah, I'll take it.

255
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:41,660
I see you've become quite adept. Huh?

256
00:22:42,580 --> 00:22:45,280
Seems as though Enma
has met a worthy owner.

257
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:48,940
You already wield Kitetsu III.

258
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:51,017
Well, that's one of mine, too.

259
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,820
You've got to be kidding.

260
00:22:57,280 --> 00:23:00,045
Are you really going to
die to save your sword?

261
00:23:25,120 --> 00:23:26,520
It burns!

262
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:33,500
It didn't fall.

263
00:23:33,900 --> 00:23:35,460
That's one good thing.

264
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:38,900
Waro Ichimonji.

265
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:47,220
Sensei, I ask that you
let me have her sword.

266
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:49,920
Alright, it's yours then.

267
00:23:53,420 --> 00:23:57,520
I promise I'll get stronger
for both of us, Kuina.

268
00:23:57,960 --> 00:24:00,977
I'll be so strong that my name
reaches up to the heavens.

269
00:24:01,060 --> 00:24:04,825
I'll be the world's greatest
swordsman, no matter what it takes.

270
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:06,830
Boy,

271
00:24:06,913 --> 00:24:08,857
have you not questioned
why the famed blade Lady

272
00:24:08,940 --> 00:24:11,822
Hiyori left you feel so
comfortable in your hand?

273
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:15,097
It works much like a cursive blade does.

274
00:24:15,180 --> 00:24:17,140
The weak cannot handle them.

275
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:22,284
Though there is a much bigger reason why
it feels familiar to you as you wield it.

276
00:24:22,900 --> 00:24:24,488
You may find this shocking,

277
00:24:24,620 --> 00:24:28,557
but your Wado Ichimonji and Enma
were crafted by the very same man.

278
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:32,080
He was the legendary
blacksmith Shimoski Kozaburo.

279
00:24:42,300 --> 00:24:45,260
I never thought to question
this sword's origin.

280
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:52,797
But how did a blade from
the land of Wano end

281
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:55,527
up in the east blue in
the middle of nowhere?

282
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:12,040
Oh, my God.

283
00:25:32,080 --> 00:25:34,080
Got all your swords back, go!

284
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:36,904
The Imperial Slings and Arrows!

285
00:25:41,220 --> 00:25:42,050
Enma!

286
00:26:08,860 --> 00:26:11,640
A sword from the land of Wano.

287
00:26:15,580 --> 00:26:19,000
A sword from the land of Wano.

288
00:26:22,020 --> 00:26:22,850
Zorojuro.

289
00:26:23,660 --> 00:26:25,420
The word Tsunachi.

290
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:29,137
Okiku advised me against using it.

291
00:26:29,220 --> 00:26:30,820
It's just a saying.

292
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:34,117
Some old guy from my
village told me years back.

293
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:36,376
Can't really say I've used it myself.

294
00:26:40,980 --> 00:26:42,780
That old man from the village.

295
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:56,800
He was always sitting by
himself looking at the sea.

296
00:26:58,460 --> 00:27:00,107
I didn't even know his name.

297
00:27:00,820 --> 00:27:02,720
But he told me all these things

298
00:27:51,020 --> 00:27:55,196
Sonachi, it is a word that means good
luck and can uplift your spirits.

299
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:56,590
Huh?

300
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:59,280
My spirits are doing fine, thanks.

301
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:01,477
I don't need any weird tricks.

302
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:05,560
So anyway, I wanted to ask you,
did you used to be a samurai?

303
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:08,997
Because that's what everyone
at the dojo is saying.

304
00:28:09,080 --> 00:28:10,740
Then tell them to shut up.

305
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:14,136
If word gets out, then the
Navy's gonna come knocking.

306
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:17,617
I don't get it.

307
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:18,820
The Navy?

308
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:20,220
I'm done talking.

309
00:28:20,540 --> 00:28:22,011
Go home, you little shit.

310
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:25,600
What's your deal, you old weirdo?

311
00:28:33,140 --> 00:28:35,960
Dojo kick you out, or are you just bored?

312
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:38,737
I came here to get some
more sword practice.

313
00:28:38,820 --> 00:28:41,460
Kuina kicked my butt,
like she always does.

314
00:28:44,320 --> 00:28:45,150
Huh?

315
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:48,240
But I can't pay for these.

316
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:49,920
You can have them.

317
00:28:53,760 --> 00:28:55,054
They're blunt, though.

318
00:28:55,680 --> 00:28:56,660
A damn shame.

319
00:28:57,900 --> 00:29:04,080
Everything I make these days turns out
like that, but they're fine for practice

320
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:14,860
Listen up kid a sword is not a knife.

321
00:29:14,980 --> 00:29:16,451
It's made to kill people.

322
00:29:16,680 --> 00:29:19,268
It's an instrument of
death and nothing else

323
00:29:22,180 --> 00:29:26,580
The job of a swordsmith is to make
their blades as deadly as possible.

324
00:29:27,320 --> 00:29:28,577
We deal in murder.

325
00:29:28,660 --> 00:29:33,537
Every sword has its own personality
and some are quite willful.

326
00:29:33,620 --> 00:29:35,977
It's a swordsman's job to tame them.

327
00:29:36,060 --> 00:29:40,380
If a sword is too dangerous,
people say it's cursed.

328
00:29:41,140 --> 00:29:42,557
What a load of crap!

329
00:29:42,640 --> 00:29:44,877
That's a sign of quality.

330
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:47,180
Only the weak fear it.

331
00:29:47,900 --> 00:29:49,841
A swordsman bends it to his will.

332
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:53,180
Calling it cursed is a badge of honor.

333
00:29:54,100 --> 00:29:55,780
Swords should be terrifying.

334
00:29:56,260 --> 00:29:58,380
Their only purpose is to take lives.

335
00:29:58,620 --> 00:30:00,780
After all, they yearn for it.

336
00:30:04,100 --> 00:30:06,865
There was a sword that
I made when I was young.

337
00:30:07,020 --> 00:30:08,260
A true masterpiece.

338
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:13,360
In all my years since, I've
never been able to top it.

339
00:30:13,800 --> 00:30:16,280
The sword had a stern personality.

340
00:30:17,180 --> 00:30:21,120
When you held it in your hand,
it set a shiver down your spine.

341
00:30:21,520 --> 00:30:23,560
That's how fine a blade it was.

342
00:30:26,620 --> 00:30:30,340
It's named after the great
king who presides over hell.

343
00:30:43,420 --> 00:30:46,400
The great king who presides over hell.

344
00:30:59,220 --> 00:31:01,200
The village was named Shemotski.

345
00:31:01,920 --> 00:31:03,567
That can't be a coincidence.

346
00:31:05,900 --> 00:31:08,437
I didn't know until the
day that old man died,

347
00:31:08,520 --> 00:31:11,620
but it turns out he was
Kouina's grandfather.

348
00:31:25,740 --> 00:31:29,622
If you want me to give your famed
blade back, you got to catch me.

349
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:31,597
It's not a famed blade.

350
00:31:31,680 --> 00:31:33,320
It's just a practice sword.

351
00:31:33,820 --> 00:31:36,620
Hey, guys, I heard something crazy. Huh?

352
00:31:36,960 --> 00:31:38,117
This will blow your mind.

353
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:41,437
My grandma told me this village
was founded by a pirate.

354
00:31:41,520 --> 00:31:42,350
What?

355
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:44,520
A pirate, huh?

356
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:49,600
He was the legendary
blacksmith Shemotsuki Kozaburo.

357
00:31:50,040 --> 00:31:52,737
He broke the laws of this
country and took off.

358
00:31:52,820 --> 00:31:55,055
Last anyone saw him was 50 years back.

359
00:31:55,400 --> 00:31:58,440
That old man was a samurai
from the land of Wano.

360
00:31:59,740 --> 00:32:03,440
The famous blacksmith,
Shemotsuki Kozaburo.

361
00:32:04,160 --> 00:32:06,480
Fine swords watch us humans closely.

362
00:32:06,860 --> 00:32:09,137
Maybe they're looking
for the right partner.

363
00:32:09,220 --> 00:32:10,380
They're patient.

364
00:32:12,320 --> 00:32:15,800
But in the end, they say
the sword chooses the owner.

365
00:32:27,560 --> 00:32:28,880
You chose me.

366
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:32,460
You came to me because
you wanted to test me.

367
00:32:38,220 --> 00:32:40,080
The sword doesn't have malice.

368
00:32:40,380 --> 00:32:42,800
It isn't doing this to harm me.

369
00:32:48,560 --> 00:32:51,089
Guess that means my
power is still lacking.

370
00:32:53,340 --> 00:32:57,811
Odin willed you with ease, even though
you took away so much Haki from me.

371
00:32:58,200 --> 00:32:59,965
I wish I could have seen that.

372
00:33:00,920 --> 00:33:01,861
All right, Enma.

373
00:33:02,260 --> 00:33:03,300
One more round.

374
00:33:08,780 --> 00:33:09,960
We got him now!

375
00:33:10,380 --> 00:33:12,204
The pirate hunter's going down!

376
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:14,580
The bastard's in bad shape!

377
00:33:14,740 --> 00:33:15,580
Master King!

378
00:33:16,340 --> 00:33:17,660
I'm begging you!

379
00:33:17,840 --> 00:33:19,480
We want a shot at Zero Two!

380
00:33:19,920 --> 00:33:21,080
This is our chance!

381
00:33:21,260 --> 00:33:23,057
We take him out, we'll get promoted!

382
00:33:23,140 --> 00:33:25,180
Me first, I'll finish him!

383
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:30,420
How should I do this?

384
00:33:31,220 --> 00:33:33,460
I need to stabilize my Haki.

385
00:33:35,400 --> 00:33:36,960
I'm releasing too much.

386
00:33:37,260 --> 00:33:39,180
I'll die if I keep this up.

387
00:33:43,840 --> 00:33:44,670
No!

388
00:33:51,040 --> 00:33:52,320
That's it.

389
00:33:56,580 --> 00:33:58,060
I see.

390
00:34:00,080 --> 00:34:03,160
Fancy yourself a conqueror, huh?

391
00:34:10,380 --> 00:34:11,360
Yeah, okay.

392
00:34:11,660 --> 00:34:13,397
The world's greatest swordsman, huh?

393
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:16,757
Well, when it comes to crewmates,
as the next king of the pirates,

394
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:17,958
I'll need the best.

395
00:34:20,620 --> 00:34:22,020
Whatever it takes.

396
00:34:25,200 --> 00:34:27,800
After all, I made a promise to my captain.

397
00:34:29,300 --> 00:34:31,420
My captain and best friend.
